a4131b60d6abb82f454722b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T09:03:44Z","email":"barrientosd9@gmail.com","name":"Daniel Ramirez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T09:03:44Z","email":"barrientosd9@gmail.com","name":"Daniel Ramirez"},"message":"fix(slides): restore mermaid diagram rendering with single source of truth\n\nRoot cause 1: sections redefined slide metadata with plain-text strings\n(e.g. \"features → hooks → store → domain\") instead of valid mermaid syntax,\ncausing UnknownDiagramError crashes in production.\n\nRoot cause 2: rslib dev default lazyCompilation caused `import(\"mermaid\")` to\nhang silently across the MF boundary (host :3002 → remote :3001) in local dev.\n\n- Add SlideMeta type in sections/types.ts\n- Extract slide metadata (title, type, diagram) into .slide.meta.ts files\n  for cleanArchitectureInTheShell, dataFlow, hostAndRemote,\n  hostConfiguration, remoteConfiguration\n- Convert affected .slide.tsx files to default-export Content only\n- Update shell, overview, module-federation sections to spread meta +\n  lazy-load Content — no more metadata duplication\n- Disable lazyCompilation for dynamic imports in ui-components rslib config\n- Add .catch handler to Diagram so future mermaid failures surface in console\n  instead of being swallowed","tree":{"sha":"9e05a71abb931db2ef241878ee481841523136a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hyperxq/modular-frontend-architecture/git/trees/9e05a71abb931db2ef241878ee481841523136a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hyperxq/modular-frontend-architecture/git/commits/36d25c1f74c3df150a4131b60d6abb82f454722b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22332354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperxq/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperxq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hype