ations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aukevanoost","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/native-federation/angular-adapter/commits/8b7ebcb97536b01c3caf7e9ffb091d35df83127c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:19:18Z","email":"auke.v.o@hotmail.com","name":"Aukevanoost"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:19:18Z","email":"auke.v.o@hotmail.com","name":"Aukevanoost"},"message":"fix(builders): resolve outputs and esbuild hashes against workspaceRoot\n\nWhen ng build runs from a subdirectory, process.cwd() differs from the\nworkspace root. Output cleanup passed the relative outputPath straight to\nrmSync/mkdirSync, so it cleared a folder under cwd and left stale files in\nthe real dist. The federation esbuild contexts left absWorkingDir unset,\nso it defaulted to cwd and byte-identical bundles got different hashed\nnames depending on where the build was started.\n\nThe dev SSR bridge also joined the relative browser path onto cwd; the\nbuilder now hands it an absolute path.\n\nBumps @softarc/native-federation to ~4.7.1, which resolves core''s own\npaths against workspaceRoot (native-federation-core#161).\n\nCloses #147","tree":{"sha":"c6608393754d4b84ce8513f5e7a6c522f9de376a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/native-federation/angular-adapter/git/trees/c6608393754d4b84ce8513f5e7a6c522f9de376a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/native-federation/angular-adapter/git/commits/8b7ebcb97536b01c3caf7e9ffb091d35df83127c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"