1a7c45beae4d74052cbde7cd8a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-04T23:20:23Z","email":"anuragkr29@gmail.com","name":"Anurag Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-04T23:21:37Z","email":"anuragkr29@gmail.com","name":"Anurag Kumar"},"message":"docs: add README and contribution guidelines\n\n- Create comprehensive README with problem statement and solution\n- Add badges for key technologies (Vite, React, TypeScript, Docker)\n- Document quick start guide for development and production\n- Include architecture diagrams showing dev vs production flow\n- Explain CSS isolation strategy and future migration path\n- Add CONTRIBUTING.md with code style, commit message guidelines\n\nThe README serves as the project''s landing page, clearly\nexplaining what problem this solves, who it''s for, and how\nto get started in under 5 minutes.\n\ndocs: add comprehensive documentation for architecture and workflows\n\nAdd detailed documentation covering all aspects of the project:\n\n- ARCHITECTURE.md: Deep dive into design decisions, module federation\n  configuration, build process, and security considerations\n\n- LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT.md: HMR setup guide, development workflow\n  best practices, debugging tips, and common issue solutions\n\n- PRODUCTION-DEPLOYMENT.md: Docker configuration explained, Nginx\n  routing strategy, CI/CD integration examples, and scaling guidance\n\n- USE-CASES.md: Detailed scenarios where this pattern excels,\n  when NOT to use it, and a decision framework for evaluation\n\nEach document provides practical guidance for developers to\nunderstand, contribute to, and extend the architecture.","tree":{"sha":"a4038a02e3a43f39a759b8bc3d158e6200740412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anuragkr29/vite-module-federation-monorepo/git/trees/a4038a02e3a43f39a759b8bc3d158e6200740412"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anuragkr29/vite-module-federation-monorepo/git/commits/03a23c57e199d1a7c45beae4d74052cbde7cd8a9","verification":{"payload":null