VXNlcjUzNTc5ODg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumaratul60","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kumaratul60/System-Design/commits/4f3f46b269ff5db0c78221a8be45ff6951f03423/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T05:17:43Z","email":"atulreso1@gmail.com","name":"Atul Kumar Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T05:17:43Z","email":"atulreso1@gmail.com","name":"Atul Kumar Awasthi"},"message":"feat: add comprehensive ESLint guides for accessibility, TypeScript, React, Storybook, i18n, code quality, testing, and production configurations\n\n- Introduced 01-a11y-strict.md for strict accessibility linting with jsx-a11y rules.\n- Added 02-typescript-typechecked.md for TypeScript strict type-checking and linting rules.\n- Created 03-react-hooks-compiler.md focusing on React hooks and compiler integration.\n- Developed 04-storybook-a11y-automation.md for automated accessibility testing in Storybook.\n- Implemented 05-i18n-formatjs.md to enforce internationalization best practices.\n- Established 06-code-quality-imports.md to prevent circular dependencies and enforce import quality.\n- Launched 07-testing-security.md for testing library best practices and security rules.\n- Formulated 08-overrides-monorepo.md for granular ESLint overrides in monorepo setups.\n- Compiled 09-production-configs.md with ready-to-use ESLint configurations for modern and legacy setups.\n- Added README.md as a modular architecture guide for the entire ESLint suite.","tree":{"sha":"0969c6be7a96f48f1ff14639a13423b98ae47e8f","url":"https://a